## Assumptions

### A1: Data Availability
**Assumption:** CSV data files exist in `/data` directory with complete OHLCV data
**Risk if wrong:** Cannot test or develop without real data
**Validation:** ✅ VALIDATED - CSV files confirmed to exist with complete data

### A2: Browser Compatibility
**Assumption:** Target modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari latest versions)
**Risk if wrong:** May need polyfills or compatibility layers
**Validation:** Document browser requirements

### A3: Data Volume
**Assumption:** CSV files contain 1-minute data, potentially years of history
**Risk if wrong:** Performance issues if data volume is much larger
**Validation:** Test with real data volume early

### A4: Single Symbol Display
**Assumption:** UI displays one symbol (MHImain) at a time, no multi-symbol view needed initially
**Risk if wrong:** Architecture may need to support multiple symbols
**Validation:** Clarify with user

### A5: Desktop-First Design
**Assumption:** Primary use case is desktop browser, mobile is secondary
**Risk if wrong:** May need more mobile optimization
**Validation:** Implement responsive design but prioritize desktop

### A6: Real-Time Data Frequency
**Assumption:** Real-time tick data arrives at reasonable frequency (< 100 ticks/second)
**Risk if wrong:** May need more aggressive data throttling/aggregation
**Validation:** Test with vnpy data rates in Phase 6

